precept RestaurantWaitlist

# A front-of-house waitlist with one active call at a time. Parties join the queue
# in Accepting; the host calls the next party, which moves the waitlist into Seating
# until that party is seated; then the cycle resumes. Service can close at any time
# and reopen later without losing the existing queue.
#
# Free-Construction: the waitlist exists as a long-lived shift artifact; no party
# identity is captured at creation. Parties flow through via JoinWaitlist events.

# Currently-calling party — set when SeatNextParty dequeues, cleared on MarkSeated.
field CurrentParty as string optional maxlength 200 editable
field LastCalledParty as string optional maxlength 200

# Estimated wait — 10 minutes per party in the queue. Updated whenever the queue changes.
field EstimatedWaitMinutes as integer default 0 nonnegative

# Service status — false while Closed, true otherwise.
field WalkInOpen as boolean default true

# The waiting queue itself — FIFO of party names.
field PartyQueue as queue of string maxlength 200

# States
state Accepting initial
state Seating
state Closed

# CurrentParty has no meaning while accepting new parties — the host is between calls.
in Accepting, Closed omit CurrentParty

# State ensures
in Seating ensure CurrentParty is set because "The Seating state must name the party currently being seated — without it the host has no record of who was just called"

# Events
event JoinWaitlist(PartyName as string notempty maxlength 200)
event SeatNextParty
event MarkSeated
event CloseService
event ReopenService

# A party joins — the queue grows and the wait time updates.
from Accepting on JoinWaitlist
    -> enqueue PartyQueue JoinWaitlist.PartyName
    -> set EstimatedWaitMinutes = PartyQueue.count * 10
    -> no transition

# Call the next party — peek captures the name into LastCalledParty before dequeue
# removes it; the dequeue then writes the same party into CurrentParty for Seating.
from Accepting on SeatNextParty when PartyQueue.count > 0
    -> set LastCalledParty = PartyQueue.peek
    -> dequeue PartyQueue into CurrentParty
    -> transition Seating
from Accepting on SeatNextParty
    -> reject "No party is currently waiting — the queue is empty"

# Party seated — resume accepting. CurrentParty is omitted in Accepting, so the
# state-exit clear below drops it as the waitlist leaves Seating.
from Seating on MarkSeated
    -> set EstimatedWaitMinutes = PartyQueue.count * 10
    -> transition Accepting

# Exit Seating — clear the active call so CurrentParty's omission in Accepting holds.
from Seating -> clear CurrentParty

# Service close — cross-cutting, fires from any state. The queue is preserved so
# parties already waiting are still on record when service resumes.
from any on CloseService
    -> set WalkInOpen = false
    -> transition Closed

from Closed on ReopenService
    -> set WalkInOpen = true
    -> set EstimatedWaitMinutes = PartyQueue.count * 10
    -> transition Accepting
